            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ischemic pain relief and survival are the targets of the revascularization treatment in angina pectoris. The authors describe the clinical and anatomic indications for revascularization in angina and the reasons for the election between surgery and percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
